# raster_fragment_blend — the RASTER.FRAGMENT blend channel, proved on the
# module zhao_raster_fragment actually instantiates three times per fragment
# (ZH-025). Run with cwd = tests/formal.
#
# TWO TASKS, both required:
#   bmc   — P1..P7: REPLACE is the source; ALPHA is EXACTLY the spec's
#           single-rounded signed lerp AND never overshoots either endpoint;
#           ADD is exactly min(255, dst+src); ADD_MOD is exactly
#           min(255, dst + unit_mul(src,a)); neither additive mode can darken;
#           and no mode can leave the 8-bit field. All are unconditional over
#           free inputs, so depth 2 is the whole property: the harness is
#           combinational and its inputs are unconstrained.
#   cover — the corners the comments claim are REACHABLE: the additive rail
#           ACTUALLY firing (without it, the min() and field bounds would also
#           hold for a blend that never reaches 255), the alpha lerp reaching
#           BOTH endpoints and moving in BOTH directions (without which the
#           no-overshoot theorem holds for a blend that never moves), the
#           unit8 endpoint (a=255 gives 254, not 255), and — the load-bearing
#           one — an exact ROUNDING TIE on the negative half, which is the
#           case a magnitude-then-sign implementation gets wrong by one LSB.
#
# SCOPE-TOTAL: depth 2 is the FULL state space, not a bound. The harness is
# purely combinational (zhao_raster_blend is three always_comb blocks; the
# only always_ff blocks hold the assert and cover statements) and every input
# is unconstrained, so the reachable state set is identical at every step. The
# input parametrisation is likewise total rather than sampled: dst and src are
# u8 because the charter §8 working colour IS one byte per channel, a is a u8
# because it IS a unit8 (spec/qformats.md §2), and mode is 2 bits because the
# field is 2 bits. Free (mode, dst, src, a) is all 67,108,864 inputs the block
# can ever be handed. There is no horizon for a scope guard to assert.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES NOT PROVE, stated plainly. The mode ENCODING (which recipe
# selects which mode), the depth/stencil/alpha tests, the tag and stencil
# write paths, the two-stage pipeline, the stall that re-issues its own read,
# and the counters are NOT proved here: they are covered by the differential
# lanes against zref::FragmentPipeline (raster_fragment_directed's recipe,
# test-mode and same-pixel cases, plus raster_fragment_random's three lanes)
# and by the mutation evidence in design/contracts/RASTER.FRAGMENT.md. What IS
# proved is the arithmetic every blended fragment in the machine flows
# through, three times over.
#
# Frontend: read_slang (the lane choice since W2.3). No package dependencies:
# zhao_raster_blend.sv is self-contained, so nothing is staged or copied.

[tasks]
bmc
cover

[options]
bmc: mode bmc
bmc: depth 2
cover: mode cover
cover: depth 2
expect pass

[engines]
smtbmc boolector

[script]
read_slang --top raster_fragment_blend_fv zhao_raster_blend.sv raster_fragment_blend_fv.sv
prep -top raster_fragment_blend_fv

[files]
../../fpga/rtl/raster/zhao_raster_blend.sv
raster_fragment_blend_fv.sv
